B20 - Enhance the security of a GitHub project

Objective
The goal of this activity is to improve the security of an existing GitHub project by applying stronger security practices.

Method
I reviewed a GitHub project and identified areas where security controls and development practices could be strengthened.

Findings
- Improved recommendations for password security and credential protection.
- Added guidance to avoid exposing API keys and sensitive configuration data publicly.
- Suggested using environment variables and safer configuration practices to reduce accidental exposure risks.
- Improved project awareness of secure development practices and repository management.

Security Principle
This activity reinforced:
- Secure coding practices
- Confidentiality of sensitive data
- Access control and credential protection
- Defence against accidental information exposure

Evidence
- Screenshot of GitHub repository/project
- Screenshot of updated README or security recommendations
- Screenshot of improved configuration examples using .env files
- Notes summarising implemented security improvements

Reflection
This activity highlighted how improving development practices can significantly strengthen project security. It reinforced the importance of secure handling of sensitive information and following cybersecurity best practices during software development.
